## Why This Is Asked
Tests basic Android data persistence and UI wiring using familiar components.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, database
- LiveData and ViewModel
- Repository pattern
- Prepopulation via RoomDatabase.Callback
- Rotation handling with LiveData

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Task(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val text: String,
  val done: Boolean = false
)
@Dao
interface TaskDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Task") fun getAll(): LiveData<List<Task>>
  @Insert fun insert(task: Task): Long
  @Delete fun delete(task: Task)
}
@Database(entities = [Task::class], version = 1)
abstract class AppDb : RoomDatabase() {
  abstract fun taskDao(): TaskDao
}
```

